<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-147] Interpreter property &apos;spark.replClassServer.port&apos; does not affect actual classServer port</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-147</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Code here &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/blame/master/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/spark/SparkInterpreter.java#L240&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/blame/master/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/spark/SparkInterpreter.java#L240&lt;/a&gt; makes initialise SparkIMain &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/v1.4.0/repl/scala-2.10/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/repl/SparkIMain.scala#L118&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/v1.4.0/repl/scala-2.10/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/repl/SparkIMain.scala#L118&lt;/a&gt; with empty SparkConf, so property with the user-set port number is not propagated. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12841899">ZEPPELIN-147</key>
            <summary>Interpreter property &apos;spark.replClassServer.port&apos; does not affect actual classServer port</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
                                            <priority id="3" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/priorities/major.svg">Major</priority>
                        <status id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/statuses/open.png" description="The issue is open and ready for the assignee to start work on it.">Open</status>
                    <statusCategory id="2" key="new" colorName="blue-gray"/>
                                    <resolution id="-1">Unresolved</resolution>
                                        <assignee username="-1">Unassigned</assignee>
                                    <reporter username="bzz">Alexander Bezzubov</reporter>
                        <labels>
                    </labels>
                <created>Wed, 1 Jul 2015 06:03:09 +0000</created>
                <updated>Thu, 10 May 2018 06:50:27 +0000</updated>
                                            <version>0.5.0</version>
                    <version>0.6.0</version>
                                                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>4</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14609706" author="bzz" created="Wed, 1 Jul 2015 08:02:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;For now, the workaround could be use &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;export ZEPPELIN_INTP_JAVA_OPTS=-Dspark.replClassServer.port=11111&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; inside &lt;tt&gt;conf/zeppelin-env.sh&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14610682" author="moon" created="Wed, 1 Jul 2015 17:31:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Currently, it can be done by exporting environment variable like, &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;export ZEPPELIN_INTP_JAVA_OPTS=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;-Dspark.replClassServer.port=11111&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-95&quot; title=&quot;Make environment variables and jvm properties customizable per Interpreter&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-95&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-95&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; will resolve this issue. Do you mind move fix version to 0.6.0 or something other?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14611260" author="bzz" created="Thu, 2 Jul 2015 00:55:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thank you, sounds as a plan! Just moved it to 0.6&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
